 "text": "Gold Mine Production History Since 1900 | USGS Data\n\n# Gold mine-production history since 1900\n\nWorld mine production rose from 386 tonnes in 1900 to 3,160 in 2022; the annual series peaked at 3,310 in 2018. A separate line shows U.S. primary production.\n\nCoverage 1900 to 2022 Primary source U.S. Geological Survey Released 2026-08-11\n\n2022 world output 3,160 t Latest historical annual observation\n\n2018 historical peak 3,310 t World mine production per year\n\nChange since 1900 8.2× World output through 2022\n\n## World gold mine production\n\nThe historical series ends in 2022. These are annual flows, not above-ground stocks or reserves.\n\nWorld output U.S. output\n\nWorld gold mine production in metric tonnes. Annual observations; gaps mean unavailable data.\n\nView all 123 annual observations\n\ngold production history\n\n| Year | World mine production (t) | U.S. primary production (t) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1900 | 386 | 120 |\n| 1901 | 395 | 120 |\n| 1902 | 451 | 122 |\n| 1903 | 496 | 114 |\n| 1904 | 526 | 122 |\n| 1905 | 575 | 133 |\n| 1906 | 608 | 146 |\n| 1907 | 623 | 132 |\n| 1908 | 668 | 138 |\n| 1909 | 687 | 150 |\n| 1910 | 689 | 143 |\n| 1911 | 699 | 146 |\n| 1912 | 705 | 140 |\n| 1913 | 694 | 135 |\n| 1914 | 663 | 139 |\n| 1915 | 704 | 150 |\n| 1916 | 685 | 140 |\n| 1917 | 631 | 123 |\n| 1918 | 578 | 102 |\n| 1919 | 550 | 85.6 |\n| 1920 | 507 | 74.1 |\n| 1921 | 498 | 72.9 |\n| 1922 | 481 | 71.3 |\n| 1923 | 554 | 74.8 |\n| 1924 | 592 | 76 |\n| 1925 | 591 | 71.8 |\n| 1926 | 602 | 69.4 |\n| 1927 | 597 | 65.5 |\n| 1928 | 603 | 66.8 |\n| 1929 | 609 | 64 |\n| 1930 | 648 | 66.5 |\n| 1931 | 695 | 69.2 |\n| 1932 | 754 | 72.5 |\n| 1933 | 793 | 71.7 |\n| 1934 | 841 | 86.4 |\n| 1935 | 924 | 101 |\n| 1936 | 1,030 | 118 |\n| 1937 | 1,100 | 128 |\n| 1938 | 1,170 | 161 |\n| 1939 | 1,230 | 145 |\n| 1940 | 1,310 | 151 |\n| 1941 | 1,080 | 148 |\n| 1942 | 1,120 | 108 |\n| 1943 | 896 | 42.4 |\n| 1944 | 813 | 31.1 |\n| 1945 | 762 | 29.7 |\n| 1946 | 860 